## x86_64 Version

An x86_64 version of the Docker image is available for systems that don't support ARM64 architecture. To build and use the x86_64 version:

1. Run the build script:
   ```bash
   chmod +x build_x86_64.sh
   ./build_x86_64.sh
   ```

2. Run the Docker container:
   ```bash
   docker run --name foundry-server \
     -p 3724:3724/udp \
     -p 27015:27015/udp \
     -v /your/path/to/server:/home/foundry/server_files \
     -v /your/path/to/data:/home/foundry/persistent_data \
     -e TZ="Your/Timezone" \
     -e SERVER_NAME="Your Server Name" \
     -e SERVER_PWD="YourPassword" \
     -e PAUSE_SERVER_WHEN_EMPTY=true \
     -e MAX_TRANSFER_RATE=8192 \
     docker-foundry:latest
   ```

This version uses native Wine and SteamCMD installations without requiring box64 emulation, making it compatible with standard x86_64 systems.
